module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.unread_member_defaults_to_a_legal_value_of_its_domain

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data unread_member_defaults_to_a_legal_value_of_its_domain: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "unread_member_defaults_to_a_legal_value_of_its_domain" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a decoder that cannot read a member substitutes a value the peer could legitimately have sent, so the gap becomes indistinguishable from data** (INVALID STATE: a decode arm for an absent, wrong-typed or unparseable member answers with an inhabitant of the member's own domain -- an empty object for arguments, an empty string for an identifier, zero for a count -- rather than with a refusal or a typed unavailability. HARM: every downstream consumer is reading a value that was never observed, and no consumer can tell, because the substituted value is exactly what a well-formed peer sends when it means that value. The wrongness is therefore SILENT in the DESIGN section 5 sense rather than merely lenient, and it is not caught by any amount of consumer-side care: there is nothing at the consumer to be careful about.)",

    "WHY IT IS ITS OWN CLASS AND NOT [[absorbing_fallback]]. The absorbing fallback widens -- it answers the SUPERSET, top-as-answer standing for top-as-ignorance -- and its cost is that it is denominated in the corpus rather than the change. This one NARROWS to a specific point of the domain, and its cost is that the point is indistinguishable from a measurement. The repairs are non-substitutable: an absorbing fallback is repaired by computing the precise set, and no precision repairs this one, because the deficit is that a value was invented at all. Nor is it [[refusal_reabsorbed_by_intermediate_default]], where a producer DID refuse correctly and a later frame swallowed it -- following the outcome through consumers is the guard there, and here there is no outcome to follow, because the producing site never made one.",

    "THE RECOGNITION RULE IS A QUESTION ABOUT THE DEFAULT'S MEMBERSHIP, NOT ABOUT ITS SIZE: ask whether a correct peer could send exactly this value meaning it. If it could, the default has no marker and the decode arm must refuse or return a typed unavailability instead. The empty collection, the empty string and zero are the three that pass review most easily, because each reads as neutral -- and neutrality is the property that makes them undetectable, not the property that makes them safe.",

    "THREE SPECIMENS IN ONE DECODER, FOUND BY OPERATOR-SUPPLIED SCOPE REVIEW AND CONFIRMED ON MAIN (2026-09-11, gunbc DSV41-3, `gunbc.harness.harness_wire`). A tool call whose `arguments` were absent OR were present and unparseable as JSON decoded to `{}`; a tool call whose `id` was absent decoded to `\"\"`; a `usage` object that was absent, non-numeric or missing one of its two counts decoded to `0`. Each arm is a different consequence rather than three spellings of one. The `{}` reaches `gunbc.harness.harness_tool`, which reads the tool's parameters off it, finds none, and RUNS the tool with its arguments removed -- for this harness's shell tool that is an empty command, and for the truncated-object case (a shape models actually produce under sampling) it converts 'the codec could not read this call' into 'the model called this tool with no arguments' and reports success. The `\"\"` is written back as the `tool_use_id` of the tool result, so the model is handed output it cannot attribute, and two calls in one round become indistinguishable. The `0` is compared by `harness_context_exhausted` and `harness_compaction_due` against the declared budget, so the two mechanisms that exist to stop a turn before it overruns its window are disarmed precisely when the usage object cannot be read.",

    "THE USAGE ARM SHOWS THE SECOND REPAIR SHAPE, AND WHY REFUSAL IS NOT ALWAYS THE ANSWER. A response whose content decoded perfectly but whose counts did not is TWO observations, one good and one missing; refusing the whole turn would throw away work the model did, and defaulting would fabricate a measurement. The repair is a typed unavailability carried to the consumer that must decide -- `HarnessUsageRead`, following the same shape the same module already used for the clock, whose `ClockUnixMillisRefused` rides into the event stream instead of a fabricated epoch. The line then stops at the budget check, which is the one consumer that cannot proceed, and the event stream records `round.usage_unavailable` rather than a `round.usage` of zeros that a throughput reader would difference into a plausible rate.",

    "RUNG. Found at mitigatable-and-not-even-that (no diagnostic existed; the arms were green by construction). Repaired to mechanically preventable: the decode arms refuse or return unavailability, and discriminating reds are enrolled at `test.claim.harness_chat_shape` -- one per fabricated arm, each of which was a GREEN PARSE before the repair -- beside positive controls proving well-formed bodies still decode and that an unmodelled block kind is still skipped rather than refused. CEILING: structural impossibility is attainable and not reached. The state is still writable because the decoder returns a domain value by hand; a codec DERIVED from the declared wire shape, where a required member has no constructor for 'not read', has no arm in which to write a default. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: a generated codec over `extdeps.llm.anthropic_messages_api` and the OpenAI chat shape -- emission and ingestion as one decision procedure read in both directions (DESIGN section 4) -- sufficient to replace every hand-authored decode arm in `gunbc.harness.harness_wire`, not merely to cover the response envelope.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
